# Bilingual Content Patterns

Content datasets in `data/` follow this shape — extend, never bypass:

```ts
type Bilingual = { ar: string; en: string };
```

- Add new fields with both `ar` and `en` values; TypeScript will flag missing variants if you model them as `Bilingual`.
- Components read strings via `useLanguage()` from `context/LanguageContext.tsx` — do not create a second i18n mechanism.
- Language persists through localStorage plus `?lang=` deep links; keep both behaviors intact.
- Numbers, dates, and phone numbers shown to patients should be formatted per active locale direction (RTL/LTR aware).
- Any new section must work flipped: verify layout under both `dir="rtl"` (default) and `dir="ltr"`.
